  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Integrated canonical BitPolynomialStorage with 64 low-to-high GF(2) coefficients per uint64 word, persistent BigUint64Array storage whenever any packed kernel is compiled, versioned minimal serialization, bulk local formatting/coefficient traversal, and source-transparent borrowed-record kernels for validation, bit length, coefficient access, population count, equality, XOR, and left/right shifts. Selective native artifacts preserve the packed carrier across interleaved dynamic operations, so a later compiled call does not remarshal stored lists; a dedicated bit-length-only artifact regression proves that repeated compiled borrows retain the same persistent carrier object. CPython, SageMath, Sage.js dynamic fallback, selective AOT, and full-module AOT execution agree at 0/63/64/65 and maximum-word boundaries; zero shifts above uint64 and malformed transactional writes are covered. Independent review compiled all eight public kernels separately and verified persistent carrier identity plus 150 randomized native/dynamic cases. The combined branch preserves its newer package budgets while adding the reviewed polynomial-kernel dependency.",
    "risks": [
      "The source-transparent compiler currently lacks uint64 bitwise operators, so XOR deliberately performs 64 arithmetic bit steps per word; a future representation-level compiler primitive can optimize this without changing the storage contract.",
      "Only linux-x64 execution was available in this lane; required linux-arm64, Windows x64, and macOS arm64 validation remains CI or integration work.",
      "The full native tier passes on linux-x64, including rebuilt production artifacts, FFI lifecycle sanitizers, matrix migrations, and matrix and polynomial performance budgets; the other required platforms remain CI or integration work.",
      "This is a disjoint core lane and does not modify the public polynomial API, production native-kernel manifest, dispatch profiles, or external NTL integration."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Adopt BitPolynomialStorage as the public GF(2)[x] canonical representation in a separate integration lane, with retained Sage differential tests.",
      "Add a generated opaque NTL GF2X resource for measured large multiplication, division, GCD, and factorization crossovers while preserving packed core storage at the public boundary.",
      "Consider a general compiler uint64 bitwise intrinsic/lowering only after this storage contract lands; this lane intentionally changes no compiler internals."
    ]
  }
}
